From 82751be91eb3ae5ebbc0ce4d5097888044e64a2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StonkGuy <68372320+StonkGuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:24:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] DiskCache: a format version of the fork's own

The disk cache key is the format version, the host features and the
codegen-affecting config; it does not name the FEX build. eac-2610
changed codegen in several places (POPF's flag handling, IRET with NT,
...) but kept upstream's version 30, so a cache filled by one fork build
was taken by the next one (and by an upstream FEX-2610 with the same
codegen config): blocks translated before a fix kept running without it.
The guest's Steam FEX tool runs with DiskCache=1.

FormatVersion is now 0x8000 | revision << 8 | upstream version (0x812B on eac-2611; 0x811E on eac-2610):
bit 15 is never set upstream, so fork and upstream caches never mix, and
every fork change to codegen increments the revision (reset to 1 on a
rebase onto a new upstream version). This one invalidates every cache
written so far, once.

InstructionCountCI: BinaryCacheVersion set to the new FormatVersion (33067)
everywhere.

eac-2611 (FEX-2611.1, upstream FormatVersion 43): revision reset to 1 as the
scheme above says; it covers the whole rebased series, so the eac-2610
revision bumps 2 (MOV FS/GS) and 3 (instructions longer than 15 bytes,
XSETBV) are folded in and revision 4 (0F B8/BC/BD decode) is upstream's
own change now. The expected-code entries the fork's codegen changes
(POPF, POP SS, MOV to and from FS/GS, the Sims 1 hot block) are not
regenerated yet: that needs an arm64 build (ninja instcountci_update_tests)
because CPUState offsets moved upstream (debug registers, c5352bf18a).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
